  "_median_crossings_doc": "ledger 0079 0.2.3 (coordinator 2026-11-05: NAIP shows Quebec's median paved where 48th / grid_unclassified_27 crosses it at (1656, 789), so pave it): OSM ends grid_unclassified_27 at the west carriageway's node (1649.2, 789.4) and starts grid_tertiary_65 at the east one's (1662.7, 789.4); no way joins them, so the 4 m between the two carriageway ribbons stayed grass. tools/trim_connectors.py median_crossings adds the straight crossing node to node, kept at any length and welded at both ends. width_m 10.0 [rule]: grid_tertiary_65's own width, the wider of the two streets it joins, so its edges meet both (NAIP reads the cross street's west approach about 15 m curb to curb, centred about 4 m south of OSM's line: the streets' OSM widths are short here, a wider question than this crossing). Also measured: the strip between Quebec's two OSM carriageway ribbons (grid_primary_6 / 7, 4-6 m, narrowing to 1-2.5 m south) reads asphalt or concrete on NAIP at 48 of 49 samples along 860 m, never planted: owed to Kevin, not built here",
